  "surprise": "P19 reversed, MIN_LR_FRAC 0.1 -> 0.3 (only edit; 4,800,000 params identical to 115) on 115-fable scored 651/655/633 on seeds 0/1/2 vs 115's 639/646/609: exact means 646.33 vs 631.33, +15.0, every seed up (paired +12/+9/+24), inside the registered -35..+35 range (central +3). Keep under the strict three-seed rule with a one-line patch; ~0.6 sd of a 3-seed mean, so not established on fresh seeds. Surprise: the gain came despite a WORSE RL start, so registered mechanism (a) (more diverse round-1 attempts) is refuted and only (b) (a more plastic handoff for the RL AdamW fine-tune) survives. The handoff was a noisier sampler, as the registered failure mode said: pretraining held-out greedy 0.9625/0.9635/0.955 (115: 0.9815/0.983/0.9845; below the predicted 0.975-0.988), round-1 Lean parse failures 17286/19025/12371 of 48,000 = 36/40/26% (115: 25/22/18%; s0/s1 above the predicted 15-30%), round-1 sample acc 0.207/0.208/0.251 vs 0.318/0.301/0.315, round-1 targets solved 647/610/684 vs 718/756/691 (mean -75). But expert iteration climbed faster: r1->r4 +484/+512/+439 (mean +478 vs 115's +384) to r4 1131/1122/1123 vs 1131/1122/1065, and eval beat 115 on every seed. The eval gain sits at lengths 7-9, not the frontier: ge10 100/104/95 vs 103/97/89, ge11 20/22/19 vs 25/23/19, ge12 5/5/4 vs 5/4/4, L* 12/12/11. Pretraining as predicted: 4238/4137/4233 steps (115: 4204/4218/4263), final train loss 0.0535/0.0537/0.0542 (115 ~0.050-0.052), final val loss 0.0799/0.0819/0.0740 (115: 0.0826/0.0806/0.0792; seed 2 below the predicted 0.079-0.088). Post-RL eval greedy 0.9855/0.990/0.9905; totals 1578/1476/1727 s. Reading: a less-annealed handoff samples worse but fine-tunes better under expert iteration, consistent with the token-format asymmetry (088 floor 0.0: -66; 077 floor 0.3: tie). Follow-ups: floor 0.5 or constant LR after warmup (a simplification), and handoff weight norms/sharpness to explain the faster climb.",
